# Python bytecode (night-dragon-maintenance-T1, the zelynic
# root-owned __pycache__ class): the interpreter writes caches beside
# imported sources with the invoking user's ownership; a root-run
# harness leaves root-owned .pyc files a later non-root teardown
# cannot remove. Ignored at both shapes - the directory and the
# bare file.
__pycache__/
__pycache__
*.pyc
